 "why_this_is_sharper": "a factor that is constant WITHIN a track and different BETWEEN tracks is what you get when the COTANGENT handed to that track is scaled: every weight gradient downstream of it inherits the same constant, and the forward is untouched. That matches what is measured -- the forward at block 47 agrees to under 1 % masked on both tracks (s 3.66e-03, z 8.82e-03) while the pair gradients are uniformly 18 % high and the single gradients uniformly ~11 % low.",
 "two_candidates_and_the_discriminator": [
  {
   "candidate": "A. our block-47 backward scales each track",
   "against_it": "blocks 0 and 23 run the SAME code on the same config and read 1.00 on both tracks; only the weights and the activation magnitudes differ."
  },
  {
   "candidate": "B. the harness injects a per-track-scaled cotangent at block 47 only",
   "for_it": "these arms are isolated -- each block is driven by the bundle's own boundary, so block 47's cotangent comes from a different place in the capture than block 0's and 23's do. A constant per track is exactly the signature.",
   "against_it": "tt_bio/openfold3_trunk.py returns s, z straight out of the Pairformer, so there is nothing in OUR trunk after block 47 that could rescale either track."
  },
  {
   "discriminator": "record the injected cotangent norm alongside the reference's own cotangent norm at each block boundary, per track. If the ratio reads 1.18 on z and 0.89 on s at block 47 and 1.00 at blocks 0 and 23, it is B -- an INSTRUMENT defect at the campaign's worst trunk result, not a port defect. If both read 1.00, it is A. The bundles already carry probe.cot_s_norm and probe.cot_z_norm; what is missing is OUR side of the same two numbers."
  }
 ],
 "correction_to_pass_128": "I wrote that block 47 carries a block-wide 1.18x inflation across \"essentially the whole block\". That is wrong on the single track, which is DEFLATED to about 0.89, and on attn_pair_bias, which reads 0.80 excluding its 32x outlier. The correct statement is two factors, one per track, in opposite directions.",
 "unchanged": "the 32x anti-correlated tensor 47.attn_pair_bias.layer_norm_a.weight is still its own defect, and blocks 0 and 23 are still right to within 5 % on 92-94 % of their tensors."
}
